# Project Context

**Code Connect** — educational full-stack monorepo (React + NestJS).

## Stack
- **Web**: React 19, Vite 8, **Tailwind CSS**, Atomic Design, Vitest + Testing Library
- **API**: NestJS 11, **REST** APIs, Jest + supertest, port `3000`
- **Git**: **Conventional Commits** (`feat(web):`, `fix(api):`, …)

## Structure
```
apps/web/src/
  components/{atoms,molecules,organisms,templates}/
  pages/
apps/api/src/     # feature modules, REST controllers
```

## Commands (root)
- `pnpm dev` / `pnpm dev:web` / `pnpm dev:api`
- `pnpm build` / `pnpm lint`
- `pnpm test:api` / `pnpm test:api:e2e`
- `pnpm test:web` — web unit/component tests (add script when Vitest is set up)

## Agent notes
- New web component → folder + Tailwind + **mandatory** `.test.tsx`
- New API endpoint → REST verbs, status codes, DTOs; test in spec/e2e
- Commits always follow Conventional Commits (see `git-commits.mdc`)
